  "why": "A mechanism on one drive: a lever turns -18° on its pin, pushes a slider along x by a law that follows its lower corner (30·sin a + 3(cos a − 1)), and a card rides the slider. The gap between lever and slider is 0.1 mm at every drive value in closed form, and the lever's face stays at least 2.1 mm from the card, least at drive 0 and growing as 8·sin a. Both checks pass; a sweep that stops posing the slider or the card it carries fails one of them.",
